 They chat all about the releases coming up, plus some more exclusive information for&nbsp;Mummy: the Curse 2nd Edition&nbsp;and&nbsp;Deviant: the Renegades. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Be sure to check us out on&nbsp;Facebook&nbsp;or through our Google Plus Community. To stay up to date,&nbsp;subscribe through iTunes!&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Links For This Episode:&nbsp;&nbsp; White Wolf Entertainment: http://www.white-wolf.com/ Occam's Laser Music: https://occamslaser.bandcamp.com/ Midnight Express Podcast: https://midnightexpress.podbean.com/ Mike's History Podcast on the Satanic Panic: http://historylessons.libsyn.com/161-the-satanic-panic Full Metal RPG Podcast: http://fullmetalrpg.com/ &nbsp; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's also mentioned about, the book is getting a Immortals section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T04:50:52-07:00","id":1304152,"title":"","content":"1e lesser mummy splat? are you talking about the Sadihk I think they were called? their still there, there 4 tier cultists","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:09:02-07:00","id":1304156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1304093-immortals-in-mummy-2e?p=1304152#post1304152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e lesser mummy splat? are you talking about the Sadihk I think they were called? their still there, there 4 tier cultists</div> </div> </div> </div> So tier 3 cultists are like Immortals like Puriefied and Eternals and Wardens and so on. And Tier 4 Cultists are Sadihk and maybe other stuff? <br /> <br /> Are Tier 1 cultists just regular mortals and tier 2 cultist supernatural mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:13:10-07:00","id":1304159,"title":"","content":"4 tier is exclusive for Sadihk, everything else as you say I think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:38:07-07:00","id":1304164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245854#post1245854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can invest your Pillars in your cultists. Doing so allows a cultist to access some of a mummy\u2019s related powers, limited by the cultist\u2019s tier. The tiers are:<br /> 1. Ordinary mortals<br /> 2. Sorcerers<br /> 3. Immortals<br /> 4. Sadikh<br /> You can also use Pillars invested in your cultists to resurrect yourself if your body is utterly destroyed, taking their body as your new one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:05:11-07:00","id":1304211,"title":"","content":"I'm betting there will be a deal of information about 2nd edition Immortals (Blood Bathers &amp; Body Snatchers were 2nd-Edition-ed up in Dark Eras books) in a more complete form, likely being a lesser related template to Mummy than the Sadikh is, as the Sadikh is more closely linked to the Mummy and its powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T15:12:41-07:00","id":1304326,"title":"","content":"In which Dark Era book were they 2nd-edition-ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T15:18:23-07:00","id":1304327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1304093-immortals-in-mummy-2e?p=1304326#post1304326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which Dark Era book were they 2nd-edition-ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Eras Companion - &quot;Fall of Isireion&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T15:51:12-07:00","id":1304328,"title":"","content":"First era in the book... do I feel dumb now. So much to read that some things always slip through....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:59:40-07:00","id":1304372,"title":"","content":"Her is a disturbing thought, Arise and their servants selective breeding mortals over generations, till the perfect mortal body is born, then at the right time the Arisen immolates itself and takes that perfect body for their own. The next best ones get claimed by body snatchers. And then the breeding process continues till a mortal with an even better body is born. Being invested with Sekhem is a scary thought, if you go rogue, the Mummy can take your body if it chooses. <br /> <br /> I hope Purified are in, they were cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T20:03:35-07:00","id":1304560,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the immortality comes directly from the Mummy the way it does for the Sadikh or if other rituals preserve the body like Blood Bathing or the like...could a mummy perhaps seek out some rare type of undying being it discovers in its long existence and &quot;collect&quot; it as a useful tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T17:27:56-07:00","id":1305172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1304093-immortals-in-mummy-2e?p=1304560#post1304560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the immortality comes directly from the Mummy the way it does for the Sadikh or if other rituals preserve the body like Blood Bathing or the like...could a mummy perhaps seek out some rare type of undying being it discovers in its long existence and &quot;collect&quot; it as a useful tool?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Mummy cults like know types of Immortal are possible, so they experiment and research the secrets of Immortality, so they can last long enough to survive the Mummy. Plus the possiblity of Immortality is a major incentive to join a Mummy Cult. I don't think comes from the Mommy. <br /> <br /> We do have a few creatures who are capable of Immortality, Vampires, Ghouls, Pyschic Vampires, Liches, Ghosts, ect...<br /> <br /> Changelings, Mages, and Vampires can grant mortals Immortality. Changelings can use Oneiromancy to grant the Psychic Vampire Merit to a Mortal, Vampires create Ghouls, and Mages have a variety of methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-15-2019, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T17:55:00-07:00","id":1305175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1304093-immortals-in-mummy-2e?p=1305172#post1305172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Mummy cults like know types of Immortal are possible, so they experiment and research the secrets of Immortality, so they can last long enough to survive the Mummy. Plus the possiblity of Immortality is a major incentive to join a Mummy Cult. I don't think comes from the Mommy. <br /> <br /> We do have a few creatures who are capable of Immortality, Vampires, Ghouls, Pyschic Vampires, Liches, Ghosts, ect...<br /> <br /> Changelings, Mages, and Vampires can grant mortals Immortality. Changelings can use Oneiromancy to grant the Psychic Vampire Merit to a Mortal, Vampires create Ghouls, and Mages have a variety of methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>they cant grant them true immortality, even mummies cant with the sadikh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T15:03:20-07:00","id":1309299,"title":"","content":"Just a weird thought, but we know the Immortals 2e is in Mummy. What if the Minor Guilds are the Immortals? The origins of different kinds of Immortals might be the minor guilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T21:35:58-07:00","id":1309375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1304093-immortals-in-mummy-2e?p=1309299#post1309299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a weird thought, but we know the Immortals 2e is in Mummy. What if the Minor Guilds are the Immortals? The origins of different kinds of Immortals might be the minor guilds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I\u2019d say that\u2019d take away a lot from many of the Immortals in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T07:48:57-07:00","id":1309642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1304093-immortals-in-mummy-2e?p=1309375#post1309375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. I\u2019d say that\u2019d take away a lot from many of the Immortals in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have to agree. It would have a place, for sure, but the Immortals things should be broader than that. And I kind of like the idea that Guilds and Scorpion Cults have a habit of picking up &quot;lesser&quot; beings who are immortal along the way, perhaps by virtue of being purpose built and inherently designed to serve the needs of eternal, undying beings and provide resources and a sense of stability to them while in most cases being even more ancient. I like the idea that the guilds have informally become a sort of immortals club, a society that provides otherwise lonely entities a wider social network with likewise undying beings (one of the only options that exists that won't likely end with you drained of blood or enthralled to an undead leach).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}